<article class="ws-sheet">
<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; Reading path</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: The Great Builders</h1><p class="ws-lede">Rulers who built their worlds in stone, law and cities.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/paths/the-great-builders">Open the path &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the stops in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the stops from 1 (earliest) to 5 (latest), by when each began: a state&#8217;s founding, a person&#8217;s birth, the date of an event.</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Peter the Great</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Charlemagne</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Louis XIV</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Shah Jahan</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Justinian I</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right dates next to each person. Their pages on the path will help.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Justinian I</li><li>Charlemagne</li><li>Shah Jahan</li><li>Louis XIV</li><li>Peter the Great</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1672–1725</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1638–1715</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 747–814</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1592–1666</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>482–565</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>Stop 1, <b>Hammurabi</b>. The path begins here because: &#8220;The Babylonian king whose law code, carved in stone, is among the oldest surviving statements of justice.&#8221; What does this stop tell you about how the story began?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Stop 5, <b>Mansa Musa</b>: &#8220;Mali's pilgrim emperor, whose gold built Timbuktu's mosques and reputation.&#8221; Find one detail on its page that supports this, and one question it leaves open.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Stop 8, <b>Peter the Great</b>: &#8220;The tsar who built a capital on a swamp to force Russia's face towards Europe.&#8221; How does this last stop connect to an earlier one?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The path sums itself up as: &#8220;Rulers who built their worlds in stone, law and cities.&#8221; Which stop shows this best? Explain your choice.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/paths/the-great-builders. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: The Great Builders</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the stops in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Justinian I <span>born 482 CE</span></li><li>Charlemagne <span>born c. 747 CE</span></li><li>Shah Jahan <span>born 1592 CE</span></li><li>Louis XIV <span>born 1638 CE</span></li><li>Peter the Great <span>born 1672 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Justinian I <span>5: 482–565</span></li><li>Charlemagne <span>3: c. 747–814</span></li><li>Shah Jahan <span>4: 1592–1666</span></li><li>Louis XIV <span>2: 1638–1715</span></li><li>Peter the Great <span>1: 1672–1725</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers use details from the pages of the path.</p></section></div></details>
